A class with only `each`, before and after `include Enumerable`
 1. Bare.new.respond_to?(:map)  (each, no include)       false
 2. Bare.new.map { } raises                              NoMethodError
 3. Shelf.ancestors.take(3)                              [Shelf, Enumerable, Object]
 4. shelf.respond_to?(:map)                              true

What one `each` bought (a handful of the toolbox)
 5. map(&:upcase)                                        ["EMMA", "DRACULA", "MIDDLEMARCH", "PERSUASION"]
 6. select { |t| t.size > 6 }                            ["Dracula", "Middlemarch", "Persuasion"]
 7. sort_by(&:size)                                      ["Emma", "Dracula", "Persuasion", "Middlemarch"]
 8. min_by(&:size)                                       "Emma"
 9. include?("Emma")                                     true
10. first, first(2)                                      ["Emma", ["Emma", "Dracula"]]
11. each_slice(3).to_a                                   [["Emma", "Dracula", "Middlemarch"], ["Persuasion"]]
12. to_a                                                 ["Emma", "Dracula", "Middlemarch", "Persuasion"]
13. each_with_index.to_a                                 [["Emma", 0], ["Dracula", 1], ["Middlemarch", 2], ["Persuasion", 3]]
14. sum("")                                              "EmmaDraculaMiddlemarchPersuasion"
15. lazy.class                                           Enumerator::Lazy
16. lazy.map(&:downcase).first(2)                        ["emma", "dracula"]
17. each.class, each.next  (no block given)              [Enumerator, "Emma"]

Core classes that include Enumerable, and two that do not
18. Array.include?(Enumerable)                           true
19. Hash.include?(Enumerable)                            true
20. Range.include?(Enumerable)                           true
21. Struct.include?(Enumerable)                          true
22. Dir.include?(Enumerable)                             true
23. Set.include?(Enumerable)                             true
24. Enumerator.include?(Enumerable)                      true
25. String.include?(Enumerable)                          false
26. Integer.include?(Enumerable)                         false

The mixin, seen from the module's side
27. Enumerable.instance_methods.include?(:each)          false
28. ...include?(:tally), ...size > 50                    [true, true]
29. Array.instance_method(:map).owner, (:inject).owner   [Array, Enumerable]
30. Comparable.instance_methods.sort  (the other mixin)  [:<, :<=, :==, :>, :>=, :between?, :clamp]
31. Shelf.include?(Comparable)  (mixins are opt-in)      false
